the
    // 'lead 3 does not work on a bunch of faceplates' report). Unknown
    // types now play through 'pluck' (or the first implemented voice) and
    // announce themselves once so the missing type gets built.
    let cfg = VOICE_TYPES[m.type];
    if (!cfg) {
      cfg = VOICE_TYPES['pluck'] || VOICE_TYPES[Object.keys(VOICE_TYPES)[0]];
      if (!this._warnedTypes) this._warnedTypes = {};
      if (!this._warnedTypes[m.type]) {
        this._warnedTypes[m.type] = true;
        this.port.postMessage({ cmd: 'warn', text: 'voice type "' + m.type + '" not implemented; using fallback' });
      }
      if (!cfg) return;
    }
    const env = cfg.env || { kind:'sustain' };
    const layers = cfg.layers || [];
    const sr = this.sr;
    const baseFreq = Math.max(20, Math.min(this.sr*.4, Number.isFinite(m.freq)?m.freq:220));

    const layerStates = layers.map(L => {
      const cents = L.detune || 0;
      const startFreq = detuneFreq(baseFreq, cents) * (L.freqMul || 1);
      return {
        cfg: L,
        wave: L.wave,
        phase: 0,
        baseFreq: startFreq,
        // Pitch envelope state
        pitchEnvSamp: 0,
        // FM modulator state (RUBBER-FM, TURBO-BASS)
        fmModPhase: 0,
        fmDepthSamp: 0,
        // Per-osc decay (STEEL-DRUM)
        perOscDecayG: 1.0,
        perOscDecayCoef: L.perOscDecayMs
          ? Math.pow(0.001, 1 / (L.perOscDecayMs / 1000 * sr))
          : 1.0,
        // LFO phase (FAIRY vibrato, FLUTE tremolo)
        lfoPhase: 0
      };
    });

    // ── GLOBAL USER OSC LAYERS (OSC 2 + SUB) ─────────────────────────────
    // Injected on top of the preset's own layers. Driven by per-note settings
    // the main thread sends (osc2Mix/osc2Detune, subLevel). This is what turns
    // the timbre-swap presets into a real subtractive synth: detuned OSC 2 for
    // supersaw/beating, SUB for low-end weight.
    if (m.osc2Mix && m.osc2Mix > 0.001) {
      const primary = layers[0] || { wave: 'saw', freqMul: 1 };
      const cents = (m.osc2Detune || 0);
      layerStates.push({
        cfg: { wave: (m.osc2Wave || primary.wave || 'saw'), freqMul: (primary.freqMul || 1),
               detune: cents, amp: m.osc2Mix },
        wave: (m.osc2Wave || primary.wave || 'saw'),
        phase: Math.random() * TAU,   // random start phase so it beats, not phase-cancels
        baseFreq: detuneFreq(baseFreq, cents) * (primary.freqMul || 1),
        pitchEnvSamp: 0, fmModPhase: 0, fmDepthSamp: 0,
        perOscDecayG: 1.0, perOscDecayCoef: 1.0, lfoPhase: 0
      });
    }
    if (m.subLevel && m.subLevel > 0.001) {
      layerStates.push({
        cfg: { wave: (m.subWave || 'sine'), freqMul: 0.5, detune: 0, amp: m.subLevel },
        wave: (m.subWave || 'sine'),
        phase: 0,
        baseFreq: baseFreq * 0.5,     // one octave down
        pitchEnvSamp: 0, fmModPhase: 0, fmDepthSamp: 0,
        perOscDecayG: 1.0, perOscDecayCoef: 1.0, lfoPhase: 0
      });
    }

    // Determine peak gain — explicit peak overrides polyphony scaling.
    // VELOCITY FIX: even when the preset sets an explicit env.peak, scale it by
    // the raw note velocity so soft vs hard taps differ in loudness. Without
    // this, peak-based presets (most leads) discarded velocity entirely and
    // every tap sounded identical. _velScale floors at the same 0.55 as the
    // main-thread path so soft notes stay musical, not silent.
    // voiceGain already contains velocity, bank trim, face gain and polyphony.
    // Apply it once to every recipe, including those with an explicit peak.
    const level186 = Math.max(0, Math.min(2, Number.isFinite(m.voiceGain)?m.voiceGain:.5));
    const peakGain = (env.peak !== undefined ? env.peak*level186/.5 : level186*(env.gainMul??1))*(VOICE_MAKEUP[m.type]||1)*Math.max(.25,Math.min(8,Number.isFinite(m.balance223)?m.balance223:1));

    // Filter envelope segments — precompute in samples
    let filtSegs = null;
    if (cfg.filt && cfg.filt.filtEnv) {
      const _segFloor = (!cfg.filt.freqRelToNote && (cfg.filt.type === 'lowpass' || !cfg.filt.type)) ? baseFreq * 1.35 : 0;   // vox331: the sweep obeys the same floor
      filtSegs = cfg.filt.filtEnv.segs.map(s => ({
        toHz: Math.max(s.toHz, _segFloor),
        durSamp: Math.max(1, Math.floor(s.durMs / 1000 * sr))
      }));
    }

    const _velBright = (typeof m.velBright === 'number') ? m.velBright : 1.0;
    // vox331: HIGH-REGISTER FILTER LIFT. Bass voices carry FIXED lowpass
    // cutoffs (TURBO-BASS 720Hz, PRESSURE 200Hz Q11...). Lead 3 is the high
    // register, so on the bass-forward faceplates its notes died inside the
    // voice's own filter (user: "lead 3 doesn't work in a lot of the latter
    // faceplates"). A fixed lowpass now opens with the note: never below
    // 1.35x the fundamental. Bass register untouched; the same voice sings
    // when played high.
    let _filtBase = cfg.filt
      ? (cfg.filt.freqRelToNote ? baseFreq * cfg.filt.freqRelToNote : cfg.filt.freq)
      : 0;
    if (cfg.filt && !cfg.filt.freqRelToNote && (cfg.filt.type === 'lowpass' || !cfg.filt.type) && _filtBase < baseFreq * 1.35) {
      _filtBase = baseFreq * 1.35;
    }
    const filtFreqInitial = cfg.filt
      ? Math.max(40, Math.min(20000, _filtBase * _velBright))
      : 0;

    const voice = {
      type: m.type,
      freq: baseFreq,
      targetFreq: baseFreq,
      glideFromFreq: m.glideFromFreq || 0,
      glideRemMs: m.glideMs || 0,
      glideMs: m.glideMs || 0,
      layers: layerStates,
      age186:0, drive186:cfg.drive||0, formantDry186:cfg.formantDry||0,
      formantSamps186:Math.max(1,(cfg.formantMs||120)*sr/1000),
      formants186:cfg.formants?cfg.formants.map(f=>({...f,z1:0,z2:0,coef:null})):null,
      env: {
        kind: env.kind,
        g: env.kind === 'pluck' ? peakGain : 0,
        peak: peakGain,
        atkSamp: Math.max(1, Math.floor((m.atkSec || 0.01) * sr)),
        relSamp: Math.max(1, Math.floor((m.relSec || 0.2) * sr)),
        decayCoef: (env.kind === 'pluck' && env.decayMs)
          ? Math.pow(0.001 / Math.max(peakGain * (env.gainMul || 1), 0.001),
                     1 / Math.floor(env.decayMs / 1000 * sr))
          : 1,
        sampSince: 0,
        state: env.kind === 'pluck' ? 'pluck' : 'attack',
        releaseFromG: 0
      },
      filt: cfg.filt ? {
        type: cfg.filt.type,
        baseFreq: filtFreqInitial,
        q: cfg.filt.q,
        lfo: cfg.filt.lfo || null,
        lfoDynamicRate: cfg.filt.lfoDynamicRate || false,
        lfoPhase: 0,
        filtSegs: filtSegs,
        segIdx: 0,
        segSampSince: 0,
        envCurrentHz: filtFreqInitial,
        envFromHz: filtFreqInitial,
        envCurve: (cfg.filt.filtEnv && cfg.filt.filtEnv.curve) || 'linear',
        z1: 0, z2: 0,
        coef: null,
        baseFreqForLfoDepth: baseFreq
      } : null,
      noise: cfg.noise ? {
        sampsRem: Math.floor(cfg.noise.durMs / 1000 * sr),
        sampsTotal: Math.floor(cfg.noise.durMs / 1000 * sr),
        gain: cfg.noise.gain,
        hpHz: cfg.noise.hpHz || 0,
        // Single-pole highpass state
        hpPrev: 0, hpPrevIn: 0
      } : null,
      tremolo: cfg.tremolo ? {
        phase: 0,
        rate: cfg.tremolo.rate,
        depth: cfg.tremolo.depth
      } : null
    };

    this.voices.set(m.id, voice);
